txf|n|A pigsty. ; The common heron; -- so called from its note. ; Unbounded by restrictions, limitations, etc.; free. ; Free in uttering one's real sentiments; not reserved; using no disguise; candid; ingenuous; as, a frank nature, conversation, manner, etc. ; Liberal; generous; profuse. ; Unrestrained; loose; licentious; -- used in a bad sense.	a:1c22,24,3~1c22,24,3
txf|a|The privilege of sending letters or other mail matter, free of postage, or without charge; also, the sign, mark, or signature denoting that a letter or other mail matter is to free of postage. ; A member of one of the German tribes that in the fifth century overran and conquered Gaul, and established the kingdom of France. ; A native or inhabitant of Western Europe; a European; -- a term used in the Levant. ; A French coin. See Franc.	j:l8b,71,7~l8b,71,7
