tzg|n|The state of being free; exemption from the power and control of another; liberty; independence. ; Privileges; franchises; immunities. ; Exemption from necessity, in choise and action; as, the freedom of the will. ; Ease; facility; as, he speaks or acts with freedom. ; Frankness; openness; unreservedness. ; Improper familiarity; violation of the rules of decorum; license. ; Generosity; liberality.	a:es,61,27;1c22,35,23;1cca,26,6;1xt5,4,3~es,61,27;1c22,35,23;1cca,26,6;1xt5,4,3	v:ag5,46,3;es,24,2~ag5,46,3;es,24,2	n:es,24,2~es,24,2
